nswer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621013} {:answer/id #uuid "49dc7ab4-7db8-57bb-b1ae-604ea2d50aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621017} {:answer/id #uuid "83e12c58-eae8-5ca3-b686-3eb96d4d6436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621029} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2669d2-fc95-53d4-b670-a2994747d275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621030} {:answer/id #uuid "fa959e55-9b20-5384-bf6c-1ab954a86f60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49dc7ab4-7db8-57bb-b1ae-604ea2d50aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621017} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bda75ad-8faa-53e4-ac47-82b0b2f9c4bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621021}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e35e6e3f-2930-5eb2-9e9d-66671f71b9ff" :question/problem "![](images/48/4821bc83cdd5e8b5d7353fc822b11bdf0ae4481abe53c4de3d903578a1027d2d.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the speed of cars $A$ and $B$ as a function of the distance that they traveled during a brake test. At which distance, in meters, did both cars reach the same speed?" :question/worked-solution "The cars have the same speed when the two graphs intersect.\n\n![](images/97/978630957da7d19a233cf42bab2a8cbdeadf2fa5b444e148026e9c872b4121ca.png)\n\nIn this case, we have the point $(80,50)$. So, both cars have the same speed ($50\\,\\textrm{km/h}$) at a distance of $80$ meters."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186631093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2da3580a-6a1a-5e38-bcab-bd35f1ea5a6e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Value of a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "810244e4-2b31-5db5-bf54-f9c4993c9752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "810244e4-2b31-5db5-bf54-f9c4993c9752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631097} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dfaa1c8-2c83-5f8a-bef6-240a9647dd8c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631096}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63fcd65e-0cb2-5b99-9d2c-a65ac5fd5e2b" :question/problem "Maria and John agreed to increase the bet. Maria's original payoff matrix was\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nAfter increasing the bet, her payoff matrix became\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 12 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 12 & -12 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nThis new matrix is obtained from $P$ using the scalar multiplication $kP$, where $k=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To express $kP,$ we multiply each entry of $P$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kP & =k\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3k & -3k \\\\ -3k & 0 & 3k \\\\ 3k & -3k & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the value given for $kP$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3k & -3k \\\\ -3k & 0 & 3k \\\\ 3k & -3k & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 12 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 12 & -12 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the elements in row $2$ and column $3$, $3k$ and $12.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k & =12 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would get the same result by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186631095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2da3580a-6a1a-5e38-bcab-bd35f1ea5a6e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Value of a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b83c5a1-5528-557c-89fc-9e6884805cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b83c5a1-5528-557c-89fc-9e6884805cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631089} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a7aaf32-31fd-506a-ab23-7d7d6d7d3e33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631090}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "790dc5a5-d407-59df-b43d-9ca883392535" :question/problem "If \n\n$$\nkB=\\begin{bmatrix}-45 & 20 & 55\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n,\nwhere \n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 4 & 11\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To express $kB,$ we multiply each entry of $B$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kB & =k\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 4 & 11\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9k & 4k & 11k\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kB$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-9k & 4k & 11k\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-45 & 20 & 55\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the elements in row $1$ and column $3$, $11k$ and $55.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11k & =55 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186631099 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2da3580a-6a1a-5e38-bcab-bd35f1ea5a6e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Value of a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d5f3966-5e33-504b-a517-42083a5b636a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d5f3966-5e33-504b-a517-42083a5b636a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631091} :answer-field/id #uuid "fda1824e-4d75-5461-9442-65c1212b2906" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631106}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92694a5b-d24b-5a05-b6ed-5bed5bc9dab4" :question/problem "Chelsea and Alessandro agreed to increase the bet. Her original payoff matrix was\n\n$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 9 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -9 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 9 & 9 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAfter increasing, Chelsea's payoff matrix became\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 72 & 72 & -72 \\\\ -72 & 0 & 72 & -72 \\\\ -72 & -72 & 0 & -72 \\\\ 72 & 72 & 72 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis new matrix is obtained from matrix $P$ using the scalar multiplication $kP$, where $k=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To express $kP,$ we multiply each entry of $P$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kP & =k\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 & 9 & -9 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 9 & -9 \\\\ -9 & -9 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 9 & 9 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9k & 9k & -9k \\\\ -9k & 0 & 9k & -9k \\\\ -9k & -9k & 0 & -9k \\\\ 9k & 9k & 9k & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the value given for $kP$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9k & 9k & -9k \\\\ -9k & 0 & 9k & -9k \\\\ -9k & -9k & 0 & -9k \\\\ 9k & 9k & 9k & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ ={} & \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 72 & 72 & -72 \\\\ -72 & 0 & 72 & -72 \\\\ -72 & -72 & 0 & -72 \\\\ 72 & 72 & 72 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the elements in row $4$ and column $3$, $9k$ and $72.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9k & =72 \\\\ k & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would get the same result by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186631102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2da3580a-6a1a-5e38-bcab-bd35f1ea5a6e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Value of a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9353430-f373-50b8-885b-bd5b5a267b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9353430-f373-50b8-885b-bd5b5a267b2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631101} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb7b8825-c901-5ba8-9746-d79d08910eff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631105}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cbffa7e9-68f2-5714-9601-1379f6895366" :question/problem "Maria and John agreed to increase the bet. Maria's original payoff matrix was\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nAfter increasing the bet, her payoff matrix became\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -56 & 56 \\\\ 56 & 0 & -56 \\\\ -56 & 56 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nThis new matrix is obtained from $P$ using the scalar multiplication $kP$, where $k=$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To express $kP,$ we multiply each entry of $P$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kP & =k\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -8 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -8k & 8k \\\\ 8k & 0 & -8k \\\\ -8k & 8k & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the value given for $kP$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -8k & 8k \\\\ 8k & 0 & -8k \\\\ -8k & 8k & 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -56 & 56 \\\\ 56 & 0 & -56 \\\\ -56 & 56 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the elements in row $2$ and column $3$, $-8k$ and $-56.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8k & =-56 \\\\ k & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would get the same result by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186631103 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2da3580a-6a1a-5e38-bcab-bd35f1ea5a6e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Value of a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09cbe4d8-edfc-5bb5-84a6-0ba7be1f0155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631088} {:answer/id #uuid "43948855-44fd-588f-8d51-601ccae8262a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631092} {:answer/id #uuid "7821608d-b88f-5c9a-9741-cbf9665b181f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631094} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf89133-b80e-59d2-8d1e-624bbec4ddfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631098} {:answer/id #uuid "b7ce5448-721d-5900-bf26-546076e61ce1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09cbe4d8-edfc-5bb5-84a6-0ba7be1f0155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631088} :answer-field/id #uuid "f350ee3d-6d4b-56b8-8078-571116e5f63c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186631104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eefdb8c8-8624-5aac-886d-e8f16b08d649" :question/problem "If \n\n$$\nkA=\\begin{bmatrix}-50 & 15 & 25\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n,\nwhere \n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nand $k$ is a scalar, calculate the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "To express $kA,$ we multiply each entry of $A$ by $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10k & 3k & 5k\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the above result equal to the matrix given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-10k & 3k & 5k\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-50 & 15 & 25\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the elements in row $1$ and column $1$, $-10k$ and $-50.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10k & =-50 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632107 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "383c9cf4-9999-544c-9991-3e389d1e8202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{13/4}}{6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632105} {:answer/id #uuid "ab127b7a-c644-50b9-bc45-4f314b20034a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{13/4}}{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632115} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4352af-5818-5677-9495-de1a6e17db7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{11} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632116} {:answer/id #uuid "b947531c-3eee-5e80-84c9-04e32ec0a073" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{7/4}}{6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632118} {:answer/id #uuid "d907ffd1-f01c-539b-a1de-9df33d4a67e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d907ffd1-f01c-539b-a1de-9df33d4a67e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632122} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c2dc46f-f898-5487-b33d-e094e125e98f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632106}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "477b81fd-0d41-5aeb-9d0d-bfba79f45ad8" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{3/4}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{3}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3/4+1}}{(\\frac{3}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/4}}{\\left(\\frac{7}{4}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{4{x}^{7/4}}{7}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{7}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7/4})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{7}\\cdot \\frac{7}{4}{x}^{7/4-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{3/4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632110 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02f8b77e-17f1-5387-a87d-23a3ff99934a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{1/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632098} {:answer/id #uuid "12bd4168-b5bc-5325-b188-fea546b91b46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632099} {:answer/id #uuid "32e4276b-e685-51a3-8475-846db1f81282" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{1/3}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632103} {:answer/id #uuid "c83531c0-b308-538b-9af3-84d795465990" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632120} {:answer/id #uuid "d5440c18-c6db-51ff-ae2c-962a62da086d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{1/3}}{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c83531c0-b308-538b-9af3-84d795465990" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632120} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b4df830-d99b-539d-9e07-f753f79c3cf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632108}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "757ec083-21ed-5196-b6d1-4055aef04474" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{1/3}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/3+1}}{(\\frac{1}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/3}}{\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4/3})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}{x}^{4/3-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70bf4863-92e7-5e95-9fd6-c2a589917968" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70bf4863-92e7-5e95-9fd6-c2a589917968" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632109} :answer-field/id #uuid "b84da965-e3fc-5ba0-9917-0cb5af5d27bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632117}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b882599-473b-551d-be43-1f32e525912f" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{5/4}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{5}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{5/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4+1}}{(\\frac{5}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/4}}{\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{4{x}^{9/4}}{9}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{9}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{9/4})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{9}\\cdot \\frac{9}{4}{x}^{9/4-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{5/4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632114 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec493b07-43f5-5006-bf2b-4faff02253cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec493b07-43f5-5006-bf2b-4faff02253cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632124} :answer-field/id #uuid "78fa16cd-fb2e-5d4f-8ed2-80a699116f20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632111}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a48b925b-78c0-5a09-affb-691438624f03" :question/problem "The antiderivative of $\\sqrt[3]{x}$ equals {{field-1}} $+C$.\n\nWork on $x>0$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "Since $\\sqrt[3]{x}={x}^{1/3}$, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/3+1}}{(\\frac{1}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/3}}{\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check our answer by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4/3})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}{x}^{4/3-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165347ea-8cc0-5126-bbd5-7fa6bd55f039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{1}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632100} {:answer/id #uuid "236f3c6d-6e65-5105-a485-32f39b7fe38b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{x}^{5/4}}{8} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632101} {:answer/id #uuid "249e2652-bbbb-5e2a-add1-2527b04b268e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632102} {:answer/id #uuid "a213afe2-4e5b-56cc-9508-969c8ab27731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{1}}{9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632113} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e3cc44-b079-532e-b82f-181f8049ee49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7{x}^{1}}{8} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "249e2652-bbbb-5e2a-add1-2527b04b268e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632102} :answer-field/id #uuid "3336ec14-fc88-58c0-bf1e-5c78ea812139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632104}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be181925-3dc1-585c-8a3a-66f07078c674" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{1/4}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/4+1}}{(\\frac{1}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5/4})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}{x}^{5/4-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22fb1199-a8f0-5ba3-94c1-4fe54d00c477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632860} {:answer/id #uuid "6217ce4c-5c47-5321-95eb-bd7ed318fcb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632870} {:answer/id #uuid "ded7b2d4-2232-5456-b8ad-a4e09a853dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632882} {:answer/id #uuid "ebbc63a2-4bd6-5d1a-b89a-9756ed93e87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632886} {:answer/id #uuid "ede9003c-dadb-5026-89b2-5630fe838c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebbc63a2-4bd6-5d1a-b89a-9756ed93e87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632886} :answer-field/id #uuid "8039fd02-8d24-5a9b-b27f-0359bfbc4263" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632874}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4681a163-40e5-5445-ba23-6f719a7705fb" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5p &=-10 \\\\ p+5q &=-17\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5p & =-10 \\\\ p & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-2$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+5q & =-17 \\\\ (-2)+5q & =-17 \\\\ 5q & =-15 \\\\ q & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=-2,\\,q=-3.$ So,\n\n$$\np - q=-2-(-3)=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632873 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2afa4594-0335-50c5-baf9-664062a5c525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632861} {:answer/id #uuid "4f367be5-8de1-5871-a02e-1b656ea3fefd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632867} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7ec00d-6501-5a55-be33-d2799bc9f7a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632869} {:answer/id #uuid "c269ed65-46a6-5d56-bfb3-1ce57809c38c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632881} {:answer/id #uuid "f30c0ef4-c880-5bf9-bb4f-0c70fbceb929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f30c0ef4-c880-5bf9-bb4f-0c70fbceb929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632888} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9283a90-adb3-5f67-a506-4b57d81a5a33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632879}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e66cc4a-738d-5443-ad33-daca77ff4c3c" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5b-3a &=8 \\\\ -4b+a &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4b+a & =-5 \\\\ a & =-5+4b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $a=-5+4b$ into the first equation and solve for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5b-3a & =8 \\\\ 5b-3(-5+4b) & =8 \\\\ 5b+15-12b & =8 \\\\ -7b+15 & =8 \\\\ -7b & =-7 \\\\ b & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $b=1$ into $a=-5+4b,$ we can then find the value of $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =-5+4(1) \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a=-1,\\,b=1.$ So,\n\n$$\na - b=-1-(1)=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632876 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5ab13a8-66eb-5f89-87d2-4dc2e894cd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5ab13a8-66eb-5f89-87d2-4dc2e894cd63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632884} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c7eaa2a-2e05-5957-b576-035c3e2194b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632866} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "527b7232-1fd3-5f24-8b9a-6dc937d1b4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "527b7232-1fd3-5f24-8b9a-6dc937d1b4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632868} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a45341e-4f36-5abf-a9a6-6893f30dba17" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632875}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8bff0e3e-2036-5666-b7ce-75fff614792d" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6y &=-16 \\\\ -3y+2x &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $y$ by dividing both sides of the equation by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6y & =-16 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=-\\frac{8}{3}$ into $-3y+2x=6,$ then we can find the value of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y+2x & =6 \\\\ -3\\left(-\\frac{8}{3}\\right)+2x & =6 \\\\ 2x & =-2 \\\\ x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $y=-\\frac{8}{3},\\,x=-1.$ This can be expressed as $(-1,-\\frac{8}{3}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "037c70e5-a983-5572-b6d3-5cc94661b5f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632859} {:answer/id #uuid "2e525041-d058-5e66-aced-f9a7fde2bdbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632862} {:answer/id #uuid "45ba51a6-fd9f-5cb6-b315-4f4b80cf3ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632864} {:answer/id #uuid "9250ac5e-9551-5d92-93ae-08119ebf3678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632877} {:answer/id #uuid "aa388d1f-eb45-543c-8500-78b2d834ded1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "037c70e5-a983-5572-b6d3-5cc94661b5f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632859} :answer-field/id #uuid "6884345f-7143-5288-86d5-41f229b50f00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632871}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e90ed6dd-ee30-50f3-a3fd-20d23f868838" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+b &=-5 \\\\ -5a+3b &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+b & =-5 \\\\ b & =-5-2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-5-2a$ into the second equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a+3b & =-4 \\\\ -5a+3(-5-2a) & =-4 \\\\ -5a-15-6a & =-4 \\\\ -11a-15 & =-4 \\\\ -11a & =11 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=-5-2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =-5-2(-1) \\\\ b & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a=-1,\\,b=-3.$ So,\n\n$$\na - b=-1-(-3)=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ab5b2e8-ff3f-58ad-b87f-97436a6f302f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ab5b2e8-ff3f-58ad-b87f-97436a6f302f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632863} :answer-field/id #uuid "75854c12-cbb9-50e0-9a24-ea7ab1e94712" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0906662-2393-5770-881f-a38e5d6e5f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0906662-2393-5770-881f-a38e5d6e5f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632883} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1af3caf-0d3f-596f-a658-2d9c68a81ed0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632878}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fad041ba-7ce4-5b1b-8161-a125b46a6d63" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4y &=-2 \\\\ -2y+x &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $y$ by dividing both sides of the equation by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y & =-2 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $y=-\\frac{1}{2}$ into $-2y+x=2,$ then we can find the value of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2y+x & =2 \\\\ -2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+x & =2 \\\\ x & =1 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $y=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,x=1.$ This can be expressed as $(1,-\\frac{1}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639425 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f13c80f9-7f5d-5fec-af59-dc1689b2df6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f13c80f9-7f5d-5fec-af59-dc1689b2df6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639448} :answer-field/id #uuid "4983382b-ebc2-5938-b2f2-e6ac5feac0e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639429}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e273fc0-17d0-5973-9dcd-635a63dfbd3b" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a422cb07a0eed88f8c13aa25f0a776ea9ad4b445ab5cffc678f8b224c2ea7d7a.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{15 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2},\\qquad y=\\frac{9 \\sqrt{3} \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}\n$$\n\n$$\n0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{dy}{dx}\\big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=15 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)},\\qquad y'(t)=- 9 \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{- 9 \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{15 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}}=- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{3} \\tan{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{5}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}\\big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}&=\\frac{- 9 \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(2 \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}{15 \\cos{\\left(2 \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}\\\\&=\\frac{- \\frac{27}{2}}{\\frac{15}{2}}\\\\&=- \\frac{9}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43c69de7-aa0d-5fff-bf6c-bfc31d074a3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639428} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b0a8cc-13f5-5f73-b2bd-a07750ab6812" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{8}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639440} {:answer/id #uuid "c324a434-dcbc-5493-9ba5-78c09480e899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639443} {:answer/id #uuid "d971a232-3953-5d47-8373-3e31b7710be8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639446} {:answer/id #uuid "e724ccfa-3ba6-53e5-9ec0-928e01e587f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{15}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c324a434-dcbc-5493-9ba5-78c09480e899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639443} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a7d9675-dcc6-5f83-a4eb-c3cf3c7613e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639437}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "346360fb-2b7e-5b89-9d1b-69565549b5f8" :question/problem "![](images/8f/8f453eda11cc0af8ff36a826e896aae15465317a31cff1e2c3d4ba6598635abe.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=15 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)},\\qquad y=16 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\n$$\n\n$$\n0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=\\frac{7 \\pi}{8}$. Give an exact answer." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=30 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)},\\qquad y'(t)=- 32 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{- 32 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{30 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}}=- \\frac{16 \\tan{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{15}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{7 \\pi}{8}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}\\big|_{t=\\frac{7 \\pi}{8}}&=\\frac{- 32 \\sin{\\left(2 \\left(\\frac{7 \\pi}{8}\\right) \\right)}}{30 \\cos{\\left(2 \\left(\\frac{7 \\pi}{8}\\right) \\right)}}\\\\&=\\frac{16 \\sqrt{2}}{15 \\sqrt{2}}\\\\&=\\frac{16}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639432 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d9f658-2d46-512f-8497-a35109843d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{22}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639424} {:answer/id #uuid "361bd596-db97-5d67-8621-949743fc548f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639427} {:answer/id #uuid "60151b34-66cb-5c7c-aaf4-85897cc6c175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639431} {:answer/id #uuid "d91bab67-6f97-5121-8baa-5eb76b2d641e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639445} {:answer/id #uuid "f85124d3-2271-5844-bee4-9ef7be4bcd73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60151b34-66cb-5c7c-aaf4-85897cc6c175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{9}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639431} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4594f0-856d-5e8e-9656-9f93e4a72a60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639438}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6116808f-1550-5222-8ea6-1d7753e86570" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b1ec0b7a502b5955006203395593b7cb23eef468f8651d49182fc59095ac5395.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{33 t^{2}}{2} - 11 t,\\qquad y=6 - 6 t^{2}\n$$\n\n$$\n-\\infty <t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=3$. Give an exact answer." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=33 t - 11,\\qquad y'(t)=- 12 t\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{- 12 t}{33 t - 11}=- \\frac{12 t}{33 t - 11}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=3$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}\\big|_{t=3}&=\\frac{- 12 \\left(3\\right)}{33 \\left(3\\right) - 11}\\\\&=\\frac{-36}{88}\\\\&=- \\frac{9}{22}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08046c78-6f2a-573f-9bc4-9a765029924f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08046c78-6f2a-573f-9bc4-9a765029924f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{35}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639423} :answer-field/id #uuid "62496c7c-8cf0-5905-81df-9db5d228c342" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639433}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e1fe9fe-6c29-5949-9877-cb0eb1fe911f" :question/problem "![](images/99/99b118406eb0c67ce3c2ca8508d2223402f2d78537f09b9dad20a4844c090474.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=2 \\sqrt{3} \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)},\\qquad y=- \\frac{35 \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{2}\n$$\n\n$$\n0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{dy}{dx}\\big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=- 4 \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)},\\qquad y'(t)=- 35 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{- 35 \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{- 4 \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}=\\frac{35 \\sqrt{3}}{12 \\tan{\\left(2 t \\right)}}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}\\big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}}&=\\frac{- 35 \\cos{\\left(2 \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}{- 4 \\sqrt{3} \\sin{\\left(2 \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\right)}}\\\\&=\\frac{- \\frac{35}{2}}{-6}\\\\&=\\frac{35}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8922ab07-5ac7-5f85-bfee-c30de7f4024a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Parametric Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77e62ee4-f6f5-5214-bfca-3db82f701f18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7 e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639434} {:answer/id #uuid "8fabe51e-c6b0-56c7-9ddf-e173c3e6c3fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{7 e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639435} {:answer/id #uuid "92960c37-67c7-5890-9c42-6790e55f2c60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{7 e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639436} {:answer/id #uuid "b293b5d6-eb6e-5c21-8f48-68a20937a447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7 e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639441} {:answer/id #uuid "d85bab82-3d64-59b9-9539-f6012b9ffa7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7 e}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77e62ee4-f6f5-5214-bfca-3db82f701f18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7 e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639434} :answer-field/id #uuid "55871236-bfdc-5bdf-9f78-3b30df198e24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639430}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd27709b-4772-5d27-a3ca-800fbfef4a8a" :question/problem "![](images/9b/9b1c9f6aa0dd5690ef3d2b83f235c5676b4e59ec728a23641632460d4b0f0a08.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=7 t e^{t},\\qquad y=t^{2} + 2 t\n$$\n\n$$\n0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=1$. Give an exact answer." :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\nx'(t)=7 t e^{t} + 7 e^{t},\\qquad y'(t)=2 t + 2\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2 t + 2}{7 t e^{t} + 7 e^{t}}=\\frac{2 e^{- t}}{7}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=1$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}\\big|_{t=1}&=\\frac{2 \\left(1\\right) + 2}{7 \\left(1\\right) e^{\\left(1\\right)} + 7 e^{\\left(1\\right)}}\\\\&=\\frac{4}{14 e}\\\\&=\\frac{2}{7 e}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643388 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1356c0de-675c-53e6-bf67-44ac2692b25f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643383} {:answer/id #uuid "13aded89-25c8-5cf3-b987-9c2e34f974b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643384} {:answer/id #uuid "227a97f1-e658-50df-9596-01060e02acd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643385} {:answer/id #uuid "ec5b337e-6942-5526-92fe-237d2bc2a972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643410} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc91714-694b-52ec-816a-92c5b6b7bb11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1356c0de-675c-53e6-bf67-44ac2692b25f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643383} :answer-field/id #uuid "0736b23c-04f6-5dab-8c85-e9d4e0e9277d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643382}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c7668ec-cfca-52ff-af3f-e1d2d9a49172" :question/problem "![](images/be/be3016908a3fba5debdfa3ac512e1a8871916fa68d2b9852d82b8fbfc7ea75f5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(2,0)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31992e60-67cb-5d39-b91d-1aba811f0c89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-7)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643386} {:answer/id #uuid "559b2eb8-6f4b-574b-a17d-356799d726d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+7)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643392} {:answer/id #uuid "b294e8f5-f4ff-57bc-b46f-70e63d26d7b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-7)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643403} {:answer/id #uuid "d7048ab3-f30e-58b6-808c-6969a2d29fbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+7)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643407} {:answer/id #uuid "ed060176-70cc-5a04-9484-38900a307bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-7)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed060176-70cc-5a04-9484-38900a307bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-7)^{2}=25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643411} :answer-field/id #uuid "6092d7ca-931b-5852-b07b-0450b60b69f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643394}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5609b857-bacb-547d-8fe0-6d23d2a509f5" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6e347eee8f744be052197ac9461905e3d7eb89ea6fdaf61ce5a2299a0176c059.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-4,7)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-7)^{2} & ={5}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y-7)^{2} & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643396 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cedc47c-131e-5102-b94e-a5b34a66638b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643397} {:answer/id #uuid "a27ec7da-cc3d-54e8-b2fb-57b07e141d51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643400} {:answer/id #uuid "acf4b007-7229-5061-b59d-0166cf24d3d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643401} {:answer/id #uuid "d4f2906a-f39a-5951-b021-c51b66bc79c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643406} {:answer/id #uuid "fae13de0-c78c-577c-8ee4-8af618abb116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a27ec7da-cc3d-54e8-b2fb-57b07e141d51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643400} :answer-field/id #uuid "4aec2ac9-de08-54b3-a5ae-15ea1db22699" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643390}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82279fa1-b5b5-56c6-a1d8-90d749cb7b17" :question/problem "![](images/36/36b49f689c735249b87414fb3d994d31ec84479082bd8b1b4a1dce70d9050b74.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-4,3)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51e1a691-a946-5e3c-bcbe-74061873903d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643391} {:answer/id #uuid "9863c856-18c5-54c7-a3d1-ff041e93f432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643398} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf83dfb-4649-5a4d-9d24-abaaa7d195e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643399} {:answer/id #uuid "f346e27d-19bb-5629-8d23-8e246e118ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643412} {:answer/id #uuid "fd92d0c6-9b4e-5412-8485-bd40836d02d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd92d0c6-9b4e-5412-8485-bd40836d02d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643414} :answer-field/id #uuid "38f394f6-5080-5512-a069-241f756bcaf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643387}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c4ada6bc-f972-5f49-bbe0-7f62419c90b8" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7dfe9e153e6db4864473b9522bcfe1ae511bce97154e26b4e08050c7125ddcf4.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-5,0)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-5))^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dabd45d-9d67-5311-8019-dea8287a1f3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+6)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643389} {:answer/id #uuid "6b8779f0-3956-5875-b349-7721604f6f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y-6)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643395} {:answer/id #uuid "ade58e31-34f8-5983-b93e-8283e7bd0def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y+6)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643402} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5ee714-bce7-51fc-97a1-9a8b34a65ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643405} {:answer/id #uuid "dd91e910-aae1-5fc0-94d5-37d6c68a9de2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-6)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ade58e31-34f8-5983-b93e-8283e7bd0def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(y+6)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643402} :answer-field/id #uuid "deff8e78-47cc-5759-a937-c8914abe94e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643409}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fef50ed7-191f-5f76-9cd3-699de213a250" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9ff685b5298b604bd7fd03012e98a2237346e4eade41c27d0561d9f2b540db3.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(0,-6)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-(-6))^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+6)^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "055a6133-5178-5632-948f-b55773ae909e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4y^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{y^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671179} {:answer/id #uuid "17774358-6aa3-5d4f-a4a7-489d7953249b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y^{3}-\\frac{3}{y^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671184} {:answer/id #uuid "19e34237-6edc-5dbb-9a68-231bfbca56d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3}-\\frac{1}{y^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671186} {:answer/id #uuid "695ddf85-81e5-5b7e-be31-38be12a6acba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3}{2y^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671215} {:answer/id #uuid "c1535c46-7e97-5684-8e70-da2b906c3a10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3}{2y^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19e34237-6edc-5dbb-9a68-231bfbca56d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3}-\\frac{1}{y^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671186} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aded238-ec22-55aa-b4ff-dc7539269e4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671302}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06f008e5-5f13-5aeb-aa04-c2c8a3946dd0" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int \\frac{3y^{5}+2}{y^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$ Assume $y\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int y^p\\,\\mathrm{d}y=y^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{3y^{5}+2}{y^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= \\int\\left(3y^{2}+\\frac{2}{y^{3}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= 3\\int y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y+2\\int y^{-3}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= 3\\left(\\frac{y^{3}}{3}\\right)+2\\left(\\frac{y^{-2}}{-2}\\right)+C\\\\ &= y^{3}-\\frac{1}{y^{2}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475a837e-b25f-521c-a4d4-3724a981611b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5}{y}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671202} {:answer/id #uuid "8eebfe58-ff4d-5c8c-b6a8-2f095dfb403b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y^{4}}{4}-\\frac{3}{y}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671230} {:answer/id #uuid "ae578435-9edd-53b8-bd2d-817f1a383bf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5y^{4}}{4}-\\frac{5}{y}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671245} {:answer/id #uuid "e89919f0-57d3-539f-8997-ae60e9705480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y^{4}}{4}-\\frac{2}{y}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671274} {:answer/id #uuid "f3205476-4745-5d57-b898-cf65a514825f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5y^{4}}{4}-\\frac{3}{y}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eebfe58-ff4d-5c8c-b6a8-2f095dfb403b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y^{4}}{4}-\\frac{3}{y}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671230} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbb08c7b-8a03-5203-a28d-c9908e61aa99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671317}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e77122e-b221-5d8a-8a43-fe74ed22c60a" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int \\frac{-y^{5}+3}{y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$ Assume $y\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int y^p\\,\\mathrm{d}y=y^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{-y^{5}+3}{y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-y^{3}+\\frac{3}{y^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -\\int y^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}y+3\\int y^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -\\left(\\frac{y^{4}}{4}\\right)+3\\left(\\frac{y^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{y^{4}}{4}-\\frac{3}{y}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9e7a3d4-2eaa-5c0c-b79e-bbb854b967f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4t-\\frac{6}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9e7a3d4-2eaa-5c0c-b79e-bbb854b967f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4t-\\frac{6}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671267} :answer-field/id #uuid "e35fb1fe-a3f5-5d6f-ae8c-fbd7b24e32cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671312}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15374ade-be7d-56c6-9f1a-1fc3902b8289" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int \\frac{-4t^{2}+6}{t^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $t\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int t^p\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{-4t^{2}+6}{t^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-4+\\frac{6}{t^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -4\\int t^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+6\\int t^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -4\\left(\\frac{t^{1}}{1}\\right)+6\\left(\\frac{t^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -4t-\\frac{6}{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1746d60b-249d-5e98-8bc5-1300d3119cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5t^{2}}{2}-\\frac{2t^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671182} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0a2277-98e1-5aa1-ac7d-da384049ec46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3t^{2}}{2}-\\frac{4t^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671224} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd5da0b-3aca-5369-b06b-62d81e58b057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t^{2}-\\frac{5t^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671238} {:answer/id #uuid "c731a56b-46ca-5b4e-8502-f9bef9d43cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5t^{2}}{2}-\\frac{5t^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671257} {:answer/id #uuid "e55ba367-b093-5950-8c24-ee02ba7118a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5t^{2}}{2}-t^{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c731a56b-46ca-5b4e-8502-f9bef9d43cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5t^{2}}{2}-\\frac{5t^{3}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671257} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfefda4a-7911-5640-8768-73c3b23c0ba4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671310}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1914f415-2da9-526d-bb62-0aed631ce877" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int -5t-5t^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int t^p\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int -5t-5t^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-5t-5t^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -5\\int t^{1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-5\\int t^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -5\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right)-5\\left(\\frac{t^{3}}{3}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{5t^{2}}{2}-\\frac{5t^{3}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671326 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "319f2254-92b7-58ef-acd7-1419ed0c71d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y^{3}-y^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671194} {:answer/id #uuid "67fed129-c2e7-5ca8-991b-66ba8e939161" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5y^{3}}{3}-y^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671214} {:answer/id #uuid "79dec28d-405d-55f7-8a58-b08d95074e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y^{3}-\\frac{3y^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671223} {:answer/id #uuid "8866831a-7848-50d7-845f-184ae299617e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y^{3}-\\frac{3y^{4}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671227} {:answer/id #uuid "89d62a5b-e939-5266-9f9f-4226ab411ecf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4y^{3}}{3}-\\frac{3y^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8866831a-7848-50d7-845f-184ae299617e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y^{3}-\\frac{3y^{4}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671227} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdd4c409-b14b-532b-b48c-4fa5283869bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671308}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a227d9e-fb91-5f9f-b8c1-0006c29d6dec" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int -6y^{2}-6y^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int y^p\\,\\mathrm{d}y=y^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int -6y^{2}-6y^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-6y^{2}-6y^{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -6\\int y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y-6\\int y^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}y\\\\ &= -6\\left(\\frac{y^{3}}{3}\\right)-6\\left(\\frac{y^{4}}{4}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -2y^{3}-\\frac{3y^{4}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0db9b1c3-1e31-53f6-9fc2-1c611e2f9398" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16cbf031-ee8c-52cd-8a67-c5aea1d059b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+\\frac{4\\sqrt[4]{x^{5}}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16cbf031-ee8c-52cd-8a67-c5aea1d059b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+\\frac{4\\sqrt[4]{x^{5}}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671181} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f7d5053-5e8c-5528-b4af-1de337ea1944" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671305}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2d53fad8-6be4-5f61-b97a-358bb1ede010" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int x^{4}+\\sqrt[4]{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x^p\\,\\mathrm{d}x=x^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int x^{4}+\\sqrt[4]{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(x^{4}+x^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int x^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{x^{5}}{5}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{5}{4}}}{\\frac{5}{4}}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{x^{5}}{5}+\\frac{4\\sqrt[4]{x^{5}}}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671328 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0db9b1c3-1e31-53f6-9fc2-1c611e2f9398" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18440319-7c8f-5338-8cff-052c9e61985f" :answe