thrm{d}x=x^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int 1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{3}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(1+\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int x^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{x^{1}}{1}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{x^{-\\frac{1}{2}}}{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)+C\\\\ &= x-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0db9b1c3-1e31-53f6-9fc2-1c611e2f9398" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb02e8e2-e7b2-5f74-ba68-e2b5d8aac091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t^{7}}{7}-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb02e8e2-e7b2-5f74-ba68-e2b5d8aac091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{t^{7}}{7}-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671251} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ff4770c-9334-576f-987a-2411905b216e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd03c39d-36ff-57e6-8cc7-8339f387c296" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int t^{6}-2\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int t^p\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int t^{6}-2\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(t^{6}-2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int t^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-2\\int t^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\left(\\frac{t^{7}}{7}\\right)-2\\left(\\frac{t^{1}}{1}\\right)+C\\\\ &= \\frac{t^{7}}{7}-2t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cc018e-8ddd-51b5-8e96-cb9bc6b3c33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t+\\frac{6}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23cc018e-8ddd-51b5-8e96-cb9bc6b3c33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3t+\\frac{6}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671189} :answer-field/id #uuid "b056a03e-98bc-5fe9-a077-f828bb5d38f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186671306}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dfce6b77-8fb2-50ed-b415-ae0bec11b920" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int \\frac{-3t^{3}-6t}{t^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t=\n$$\n{{field-1}}\n$+C$. Assume $t\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Rewrite as powers, apply the sum and constant factor rules, and integrate each term using $$\n\\displaystyle \\int t^p\\,\\mathrm{d}t=t^{p+1}/(p+1)+C\n$$ for $p\\ne-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{-3t^{3}-6t}{t^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= \\int\\left(-3-\\frac{6}{t^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -3\\int t^{0}\\,\\mathrm{d}t-6\\int t^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}t\\\\ &= -3\\left(\\frac{t^{1}}{1}\\right)-6\\left(\\frac{t^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -3t+\\frac{6}{t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe constant $C$ is already supplied outside the blank."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186671344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a58c0a18-4221-50f1-b31c-ae58d099d79d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answe